invariant: INV-41
file: src/rsa_mont.c
catches: rsa_equiv_test
reason: public_by_division starts the division from the base as it came,
  without the one subtraction of the modulus. A step of the division
  needs a remainder below the modulus: its quotient estimate fits one
  word only then. rsa.c passes no signature at or above n, so every
  vector and every handshake passes. bin/rsa_equiv_test hands both arms
  the signatures n, n + 1 and all ones, and the host arm's bytes then
  differ from the 32-bit arm's.

--- old
    rsa_mont64_reduce_once(base, base, mod);
    memcpy(acc, base, k * sizeof(uint64_t));
--- new
    memcpy(acc, base, k * sizeof(uint64_t));
